{
  "comment": [
    "Presentation for the recurring-loops monitor (contrib/timers/collect.py).",
    "Copy to config/timers-labels.json and edit — that path is gitignored, so your",
    "own job names never land in a commit.",
    "",
    "session-warden's own loops (scan, doctor, reflect, harvest, scorecard, memory",
    "eval, fleet review, dream cycle, snapshot, context sync, worktree gc) are",
    "labelled by default and need no entry here. Add an entry only to rename one,",
    "or to describe a job of your own.",
    "",
    "Loop ids come from the crontab comment tag first, so the simplest way to name",
    "a job is to tag its crontab line:  */5 * * * * /path/job.sh  # inbox-watch",
    "",
    "Per-loop keys:",
    "  label   display name (default: the id, hyphens replaced with spaces)",
    "  agent   who owns it — groups the rows (default: 'ops')",
    "  cadence human-readable schedule (default: the raw cron expression)",
    "  public  true to show it on the public fleet board (default: false)",
    "  script  basename that pins a crontab line to this id, e.g. 'watch.mjs'",
    "  log     file whose mtime is used as the last-run time; ~ is expanded",
    "  source  set to 'systemd' for a timer unit that lives outside deploy/"
  ],
  "loops": {
    "inbox-watch": {
      "label": "inbox watch",
      "agent": "chief-of-staff",
      "cadence": "every 5 min",
      "public": true,
      "script": "watch.mjs",
      "log": "/tmp/inbox-watch.log"
    },
    "morning-brief": {
      "label": "morning brief",
      "agent": "chief-of-staff",
      "cadence": "daily",
      "public": true,
      "script": "morning-brief.sh",
      "log": "~/logs/morning-brief.log"
    },
    "nightly-backup": {
      "label": "nightly backup",
      "agent": "ops",
      "cadence": "nightly",
      "public": false,
      "script": "backup.sh"
    }
  }
}
